{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N1"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 136, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual input-output path where none existed gives large gains, while replacing an existing op gives smaller or negative ones."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv on the direct input-output edge removes learned capacity, so the swap is often harmful."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "In pooling-dominated, parameter-poor cells, an extra skip further dilutes the few useful features and accuracy collapses."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Cells already full of identity paths gain nothing from another skip, and losing the e3 op hurts badly."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without a direct input-output skip, a skip on edge 4 provides the missing residual shortcut."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "When a residual path already exists via e3, an extra skip on e4 is redundant and replaces useful computation."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the only conv in a pooling cell with a skip leaves almost no learnable operations."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a 3x3 conv to a conv-free pooling cell supplies badly needed capacity, giving very large gains."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", 